Our Finance Team is looking for an experienced Billing Team Lead to join the team. &nbsp;

Our Finance team plays a critical role in supporting the smooth financial operations of the business, ensuring accurate billing, invoicing, expense management, cash collection, reporting, and financial controls. The team works closely with colleagues across the organisation to deliver an excellent internal customer experience, maintain compliance and financial accuracy, support business decision-making through reporting and analysis, and continuously improve processes to drive efficiency and service excellence. &nbsp; &nbsp;

What you will be doing

• Management Support: Support the Billing and Operations Manager in delivering team priorities and operational objectives.&nbsp;

• Team Leadership &amp; Development: Coach, mentor, and manage the billing team’s day-to-day workflows, task priorities, and workloads.&nbsp;

• Performance &amp; Growth: Conduct regular 1:1 meetings focused on performance, quarterly reviews, development, and growth.&nbsp;

• Team Operations: Lead team calls and meetings, drive operational execution and performance, and support the team’s day-to-day activities.&nbsp;

• End-to-End Billing Operations: Oversee recurring billing cycles, complex or high-value accounts, and the timely delivery of invoices.&nbsp;

• Mailbox Management: Ensuring the management of the billing mailbox and enable tickets.&nbsp;

• Escalation &amp; Problem Solving: Act as the primary point of contact for complex billing disputes, system errors, customer queries, and escalations from the wider Finance group and the business.&nbsp;

• Reconciliations &amp; Month-End Close: Support month-end activities, account reconciliations, and audit requirements.&nbsp;

• Audit Preparation &amp; Support: Serve as the main point of contact for internal and external auditors during annual, quarterly, and statutory financial audits.&nbsp;

• Process Improvement &amp; KPIs: Monitor team performance metrics, track service level agreements (SLAs), and proactively identify opportunities to automate, streamline, and improve workflows.&nbsp;

• Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner with Credit Control, Financial control team, finance commercial team, the wider BE business, and IT/Technology teams.&nbsp;

• Hands-On Team Support: Provide cover and practical support for the team, taking on workload as needed.&nbsp;

Your skills and experience

